#
# Conformance case: foundation/mixrig-kind-under-role  (AC#3 — the headline case)
# AC: foundation lowering — OntoUML MixRig discipline (issue #503).
#
# Reproduces reasoning_lint.anti_rigidity_discipline: a rigid sortal must never
# specialize an anti-rigid type. ex:HonorsStudent is a logic:SubKind (rigid) that
# specializes the anti-rigid logic:Role ex:Student → logic:MixRig (AC#3). Both
# classes also trip logic:MixIden (each is a non-Kind sortal tracing to ZERO Kind
# ancestors), and ex:Student additionally trips logic:FreeRole (an anti-rigid Role
# with no rigid ancestor). The materialized violation set is therefore exactly:
#   ex:HonorsStudent → { logic:MixIden, logic:MixRig }
#   ex:Student       → { logic:FreeRole, logic:MixIden }
# — the FULL lint set, faithfully reproduced.
#
# CRITICAL: the chase seeds only from input.nq world facts, so the schema facts
# (both stereotype puns + the logic:subClassOf edge) are duplicated there in the
# named world ex:schema; these declarations are the program axioms the projections
# need.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/foundation/mixrig-kind-under-role/> .
@prefix rdf:   <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .

# Schema: a rigid SubKind under an anti-rigid Role (also asserted as world facts).
ex:HonorsStudent a logic:SubKind .
ex:Student       a logic:Role .
ex:HonorsStudent logic:subClassOf ex:Student .
